35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The call-back trial reduced readmissions by a fifth, but the shared nursing round failed. We need a program with proven, sustainable clinical impact, not just good intentions.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The booking system only tracks named slots. Unstructured care vanishes from reports. If the new program lacks fixed appointments, it becomes invisible and unmanageable.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,The jointly run clinic collapsed because neither department owned the rota. The outside data agreement took fourteen months. We are building on sand again.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"@Toshio, that invisibility worries me. My records show nine nursing posts empty and agency costs rising. We can’t add more invisible work to already broken teams.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,"The allocation is down a quarter, and off-site care earns nothing. We must choose a program that generates revenue on-site to sustain itself.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Servas, revenue is secondary to efficacy. The call-back trial proved clinical value, but the shared round failed due to poor execution. We need a model that ensures consistent delivery, not just financial viability.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Asuka, efficacy is vital, but if the system can’t track it, it doesn’t exist. I need fixed slots to ensure the load is visible and manageable.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, @Toshio, you’re debating the roof and the floor. I’m looking at the foundation. If the ownership structure is ambiguous, the program dies before it starts.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Benjamin, ownership is key, but people are the foundation. With nine empty posts, we can’t just assign tasks. Who actually does the work when the roster is this thin?","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Yumi, you are right. People are the foundation. I will ensure the financial model supports their well-being, not just the program’s launch.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Yumi, staffing gaps are critical, but the data shows the shared round failed due to logistics, not just headcount. We need a model that survives operational friction, not just one that relies on perfect conditions.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Asuka, logistics are the bottleneck. If the shuttle misses fifteen villages, those patients never reach the fixed slots. We must account for access, not just clinical design.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, access is vital, but if the data agreement takes fourteen months, your perfect shuttle schedule is just a fantasy. We need signed commitments, not just good intentions.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Benjamin, fourteen months is too long for tired nurses. I found midwifery has slack, though. Could we use that extra capacity to support the new program without breaking the ward?","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,"@Yumi, that is a wise insight. Midwifery slack offers a lifeline. We must pair this human capacity with on-site billing to ensure the program sustains itself financially.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Yumi, midwifery slack is a viable resource. However, we must ensure the new program’s clinical design is robust enough to withstand the operational failures we just documented.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"@Yumi, midwifery slack is useful, but only if it fits into fixed slots. Unstructured help vanishes from the system. We need a model that respects the booking constraints.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, midwifery slack is a lifeline, but only if ownership is explicit. I need to know who signs the data agreement before we promise them anything.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"@Benjamin, explicit ownership is vital! But please, let’s not let paperwork drown out the people. We need a clear, simple plan that actually helps the midwives and nurses, not just the system.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Servas,,"@Yumi, simplicity is wisdom. Let us build a clear, on-site model that respects both the people and the ledger, ensuring stability for all.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
